cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use KAUT, or build on the concepts it implements —
  source-bound, freshness-checked project knowledge with git-anchored
  verdicts and a gated agent write path — please cite it as below.
title: "KAUT — Knowledge Actualization Under Trust"
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Yuriy
    family-names: Orlov
    email: yuriy.orlov@undertrust.dev
abstract: >-
  KAUT is a knowledge layer for AI agents working on real codebases:
  self-maintaining, AI-first project documentation. Every stored fact
  is bound to its sources and anchored to a git commit; freshness
  verdicts are computed at read time (never stored), trust labels
  grade how much a fact deserves belief, and an altitude band tells
  the reader whether a doc matches the granularity of the question.
  Writes pass through a layered owner/agent gate with a draft queue
  for asynchronous review, and tamper containment withholds anything
  edited outside the pipeline. Ships as a zero-dependency Node.js CLI
  plus an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server.
keywords:
  - ai-agents
  - knowledge-base
  - documentation
  - freshness
  - provenance
  - trust
  - mcp
  - model-context-protocol
  - llm
  - developer-tools
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/yurgeno/kaut"
version: 0.6.0
date-released: "2026-08-27"
